ance of BMI in the broader context of obesity research and management. SEEDO's reliance on BMI underscores its role as a foundational metric in understanding obesity and its associated health risks. This relationship is crucial for developing effective strategies for obesity prevention and treatment. [Data: Relationships (7319)]\n\n## Use of percentile tables in nutritional evaluation\n\nPercentile tables are utilized in conjunction with the Índice de Masa Corporal (IMC) to assess the circumference and muscle area of the arm across different age groups. These tables provide benchmarks for nutritional evaluation, allowing healthcare professionals to better understand an individual's nutritional status and body composition. The use of percentile tables enhances the assessment capabilities of practitioners, enabling more tailored and effective interventions for individuals at risk of malnutrition or obesity. [Data: Entities (1750), Relationships (7320)]\n\n## Nuria Valdes Gallego's influence in SEEDO\n\nNuria Valdes Gallego has been a board member of the Sociedad Española para el Estudio de la Obesidad (SEEDO) since 2015, contributing significantly to its mission and activities in the field of obesity research and management. Her involvement in SEEDO highlights the importance of leadership and expertise in advancing the organization's goals. The contributions of board members like Gallego are essential for driving research initiatives and influencing public health strategies related to obesity. [Data: Entities (1747), Relationships (7429)]", "# Spain's Health and Nutrition Landscape\n\nThe community encompasses various entities related to health and nutrition in Spain, including significant studies, organizations, and public health challenges. Key relationships highlight the prevalence of health issues such as obesity, diabetes, and the role of dietary guidelines in addressing these concerns.\n\n## Rising obesity rates in Spain\n\nObesity has become a critical public h